# [MobileVLC4 fork] Single VLC engine, upgraded to VLCKit 4.
#
# VLCKit 4 unifies MobileVLCKit / TVVLCKit / VLCKit into one xcframework, so the
# two 3.7.2 entries this replaces are gone. Upstream's own Carthage manifests
# only list 3.x, hence the local VLCKit4.json — same pattern as
# ChromeCastFramework.json.
#
# Pinned artifact (Carthage keys must be SemVer, so the alpha suffix lives here):
#   VLCKit-4.0-20260805-1123.zip — 5 Aug 2026, 916 146 006 bytes
#   source: VLCKit master, Packaging/podspecs/VLCKit.podspec
#
# The SemVer key is 4.0.1 only to force Carthage to re-resolve. Carthage judges
# `--cache-builds` validity by version, not by URL, and CI restores the Carthage
# cache by key prefix — so leaving the key at 4.0.0 would have silently reused
# the previous artifact and tested the wrong engine.
#
# No sha256 recorded: the artifact was not downloaded locally to compute one.
# The previous pin was 4.0.0a22, VLCKit-4.0-20260720-1538.zip, sha256
# d9de86d0c755cbcf46c49513ff57fffcd98258f0c7dd29f3e2d23bff3860da2a — revert to
# that pair if this bump regresses.
#
# This is an alpha. Treat every bump as a small migration: rebuild, then re-run
# the playback matrix on a real iPhone before accepting it.
binary "VLCKit4.json" == 4.0.1
binary "ChromeCastFramework.json"
